Sval: Handle WebRender errors after video overlays fail to start

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2085382 (mozilla-central 7876c1cabdfc,
Firefox 161), unchanged.

When DCLayerTree::Initialize failed to set up video overlay support, it
reported VIDEO_OVERLAY through RenderThread::HandleWebRenderError. That
sets mHandlingWebRenderError and drops every later error until all
renderers are destroyed, because it expects the error to disable
WebRender. A VIDEO_OVERLAY error only disables overlays, so the renderers
stay and the flag stays set: a later fatal error such as RENDER,
NEW_SURFACE or BEGIN_DRAW never reached GPUProcessManager, and the GPU
process neither restarted nor fell back from hardware WebRender. The
other video overlay failures in DCLayerTree.cpp already use
NotifyWebRenderError, which forwards the error without setting the flag,
and this makes the initialization failure do the same.

diff --git a/gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp b/gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp
index b1243eb0b84ba..0bfdfa9171233 100644
--- a/gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp
+++ b/gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ bool DCLayerTree::Initialize(HWND aHwnd, nsACString& aError) {
   if (gfx::gfxVars::UseWebRenderDCompVideoHwOverlayWin() ||
       gfx::gfxVars::UseWebRenderDCompVideoSwOverlayWin()) {
     if (!InitializeVideoOverlaySupport()) {
-      RenderThread::Get()->HandleWebRenderError(WebRenderError::VIDEO_OVERLAY);
+      RenderThread::Get()->NotifyWebRenderError(WebRenderError::VIDEO_OVERLAY);
     }
   }
   if (!sGpuOverlayInfo) {
